# Everything text checks out LF everywhere. Git for Windows defaults
# core.autocrlf=true and actions/checkout does not override it, so without
# this the windows-e2e runner would hand Git Bash a CRLF ./hi.sh - a
# first-run failure that has nothing to do with Windows support itself.
* text=auto eol=lf
# Images are never text, whatever text=auto's sniffing guesses: no eol
# conversion and no textual diff. One pattern per line, which is all
# gitattributes accepts.
*.gif binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.webp binary
